        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Nasal symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Approximately 4 days of frequent sneezing, nasal congestion, clear rhinorrhoea, mild itchy eyes, and mild frontal pressure when bending forward. Symptoms slightly increase at work and decrease away from the office. Possible triggers are air conditioning at work or jasmine outside the patient's unit."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Associated upper respiratory and systemic symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No purulent nasal discharge, facial pain, tooth pain, anosmia, fever, or rigors. Appetite is okay; somewhat tired from poor sleep. No cough, shortness of breath, wheeze, or chest pain."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
